{"diagnosis": "Trace ends with `TRAP: cpu trap asserted` and `tohost: FAIL 0xdead` (fingerprint sha256:d52ca6bb4e44) after 2009 cycles on NOP fetch. `mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle` returned stale `mem_rdata_q` on the `mem_xfer` cycle instead of live `mem_rdata`, causing illegal-decode trap. Root cause is picorv32.v:384 where `(mem_xfer || LATCHED_MEM_RDATA) ? mem_rdata_q : mem_rdata` inverts latch/hold mux; live `mem_rdata` is valid at transfer per picosoc/picosoc.v:130.",
"patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -384 +384 @@
-	assign mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle = (mem_xfer || LATCHED_MEM_RDATA) ? mem_rdata_q : mem_rdata;
+	assign mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle = (mem_xfer || LATCHED_MEM_RDATA) ? mem_rdata : mem_rdata_q;
",
"expected": "tohost PASS (was FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP: cpu trap asserted"}

